ustry and to work but  now because it's so expensive and  dangerous to cross the border virtually  everyone that crosses hires a human  smuggler and because it's so expensive  an increasing number have to carry drugs  to less than the cost of their passage  and so the border itself has become much  more dangerous you've had a rancher  killed there last year you have armed  convoys coming across the border often  in the rural areas and so the  the net effect down near the border for  the landholders and others has just been  a big change and and that's reflected in  in politics as well whereas you know  we've all wanted and I believe still  ultimately you'll need a comprehensive  solution to this problem that has a  temporary worker plan and some mechanism  to deal with those who are here  illegally and terior enforcement until  we get better security on the border  nobody's going to trust the federal  government to move ahead on any of the  other items why does it never occur to  anybody that the border becomes less  secure the more it's policed I mean you  know as the border has become harder to  get across and as you mentioned you have  to hire coyotes or whatever right that  that has actually stopped the circular  migration not you were just talking  about I and I I've always I've always  felt that the best way to secure the  border is have to have a legal framework  for people to come and go and then you  know your resources can be deployed  against those who are doing nefarious  things on the border and if we could  return to a time like when I grew up  where there was that circular pattern  that would be one thing but I think with  the threats today with terrorism and and  whatever else I just don't think that we  can return there to have an open border  like that just does not make sense for  our for our security you know you grew  up in northern Arizona in a place where  the Mormon Church was very active and  you're one of the Mormon serving and in  office w