blic life though and the  way you know how it informs your own  thinking and certainly i always it  always seemed like orrin hatch was  somebody who you could always he was  often off the reservation with the  republicans in terms of tolerance you  know on religious issues and it seemed  to me that was specifically because you  know you're coming from a place where  everybody views you as something you  know that yes your own belief is  something odd and the  kind of internalize that I don't know I  think everyone's religion and informs  their values and it's difficult to to  decide what where one ends and the other  begins without getting into somebody's  head or their heart so I don't know how  to answer that I'm my own religion  I assume like everyone else does inform  my values but I don't think in a way  that that makes anyone uncomfortable  that's not been my experience I've not  faced any many incidents where people  have been uncomfortable that way well  you're going ahead with the Senate run  your own seat is hotly contested so what  happens next and where should what do  you think we should be looking at in the  complexion of the House and the Senate  over the next couple of years well we  have a good opportunity as Republicans  now Democrats had a very good year in  2006 both in the House and the Senate in  the Senate that means they have a lot of  seats to defend in 2012 in fact 23 of  the 33 seats our Democrat seats so I  think we just need a net pickup of four  as Republicans and and I I think we can  do it and I think we're going to need to  regardless of who holds the White House  and I obviously is a Republican or a  Republican in that seat but when you  look at the challenges this country is  facing so many of them won't be solved  just by putting a Republican in the  White House we really need a Republican  Senate as well speak specifically about  regulations the federal agencies I mean  these agencies are out of control we've  seen anything over 